  "tagline": "Wide, flowing and very short on grip",
  "difficulty": "Slippery",
  "notes": [
    "Long open curves, deliberately few hard braking points -- stopping is the hard part here, so the layout gives you room to run out of grip in.",
    "Wide road (15 m) because you will need it.",
    "Steeply banked bowls: with this little grip, camber is what holds you on.",
    "The last three control points turn back south well west of the start straight, so the two ribbons never overlap, and arrive almost in line with it.",
    "The closing hairpin is still tighter than the 12 m guideline (~5.6 m). It is driveable -- the autopilot laps it -- but it reads as a kink, and there is 38 m of clear ground around it, so the fix is to open the layout out rather than to smooth harder.",
    "Blue hour, just before sunrise. The sun is barely up and doing almost nothing; the light is the sky bouncing off the snow, which is why the fill is the highest here and the whole scene is flat and cold."
  ],
